  "text": "\r\n\t\t Voter / Elections Information | Newton, NH \r\n Skip to Main Content \r\nCreate a Website Account   - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.    \r\nWebsite Sign In \r\n     About  \t\t\t \n     Government   \t\t\t \n     Library   \t\t\t \n     Schools   \t\t\t \n     Find It Fast   \t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t Search \n\t\t\t Staff Contacts  \r\n\t\t\t Voter / Elections Information \r\n\t\t\t 2025 Town and School Results \r\n\t\t\t 2026 RABIES CLINIC \r\n\t\t\t 2026 SCHOOL SAMPLE BALLOT \r\n\t\t\t 2026 School Results \r\n\t\t\t 2026 TOWN SAMPLE BALLOT \r\n\t\t\t 2026 Town Results \r\n\t\t\t Bill of Sale for Watercraft \r\n\t\t\t Boat Registration \r\n\t\t\t Dog Licensing \r\n\t\t\t Driver Licensing \r\n\t\t\t Estimator for Vehicle Registration \r\n\t\t\t Election Results Archive \r\n\t\t\t Forms and Applications \r\n\t\t\t Hunting and Fishing Licenses \r\n\t\t\t January 1st DMV Fees \r\n\t\t\t Marriage Licensing \r\n\t\t\t Notary Services \r\n\t\t\t OHRV Registrations \r\n\t\t\t Online Services \r\n\t\t\t Vehicle Inspections \r\n\t\t\t Vehicle Registrations \r\n\t\t\t Vital Records \r\n\t\t\t Welcome New Residents! \r\nHome \nGovernment \nDepartments \nTown Clerk \nVoter / Elections Information \r\nVoter / Elections Information\t\t \r\nIMPORTANT DATES FOR 2026 \nLast Day to submit \"Petitioned\" warrant articles -  January 14th (if bonding required, January 10th) \nPublic Hearing - January 15th - Town Hall / Zoom (Snow date January 20th) \nSupervisors of the Checklist  - January 20th 7 to 7:30 pm must meet before filing period opens, for additions, corrections etc. \nFiling Period for Town Office - January 21st to January 30th - Town Clerks Office (School candidates file at the SAU) \nTOWN MEETING FIRST SESSION 6 Deliberative Session  - JANUARY 31st (snow date February 7th) - 9 am. Town Hall and zoom \nSchool Deliberative Session - February 4th - 7 pm. SRHS Auditorium \nLast day to register to vote before Town Election Day with Supervisors of the Checklist - FEBRUARY 28TH. Time TBA \nYou are required to provide  Identification, proof of domicile (residence), U.S. citizenship, and your age . \nDomicile : NH Driver's License with the correct address or Utility bill \nCitizenship : The best documents to bring to prove citizenship are a Passport or Birth Certificate. A NH Driver's License, even one with a star on it, unfortunately, does not prove citizenship. \nYour Age : NH Driver's License or Passport or Birth Certificate \nTown Meeting Second Session 6 Voting  - March 10th Newton Safety Complex 8 Merrimac Road 8 am to 8 pm. Please bring photo ID\u00020\u00020 \nNH STATE PRIMARY -  September 8th \nLast day to change party affiliation is JUNE 2nd. Supervisors of the Checklist will meet on that day. \nNH GENERAL ELECTION  - November 3rd \nALL ELECTIONS ARE HELD AT THE NEWTON SAFETY COMPLEX \n8 MERRIMAC RD \n8 am to 8 pm \nTHE TOWN CLERK/TAX COLLECTOR OFFICE IS ALWAYS CLOSED ON ELECTION DAY \nVisit Us See if You're Registered to Vote \nABSENTEE BALLOT REQUEST FORM FOR LOCAL/SCHOOL ELECTION \nABSENTEE BALLOT REQUEST FORM FOR STATE/FEDERAL ELECTION \nAll absentee ballot requests must be submitted with photo identification \n2026 Primary Democratic Sample Ballot \n2026 Primary Republican Sample Ballot \n2026 Primary Election Results        \nAdditional Resources: \nHow To Register \nHow To Vote \nElections \nVoter Information Look Up \nVoter ID Law \r\n\t\t\t Minutes, Agendas & Videos \r\n\t\t\t E-Subscriber \r\n\t\t\t Right to Know \r\n\t\t\t Job Opportunities \r\n\t\t\t Online Payments \r\n\t\t\t Voter Information \r\nNewton \r\nTown Hall \r\n2 Town Hall Road, \r\nNewton, NH 03858 \r\nPH:  (603) 382-4405 \r\n         Home \n         Site Map \n         Accessibility \n         Copyright Notices \n         Privacy Policy \n/QuickLinks.aspx \r\n   Government Websites by  CivicPlus® \nLoading \r\n\t\t\t\tLoading\r\n\t\t\t Do Not Show Again \r\n\t\t\t Close \r\n\t\t\t Arrow Left \r\n\t\t\t Arrow Right 